        ],
        'faqs' => [
            ['How much does UKCA certification cost?', 'For self-declared products, the cost is mostly testing and preparing the technical file, and a CE or CB report can often be reused. Products that need a UK approved body add its examination or audit fees. Read our UKCA cost guide for Indian exporters for the factors involved.'],
            ['How do I get a UKCA mark?', 'Identify the UK regulations for your product, test to the designated standards, involve a UK approved body if your route requires one, prepare the technical file, sign a UK declaration of conformity and then place the UKCA mark on the product, label or documents.'],
            ['What is a UK declaration of conformity?', 'It is the document in which the manufacturer declares, under its sole responsibility, that the product meets the UK regulations that apply. It lists the product, the manufacturer, the regulations, the standards used, any approved body, and is signed and dated.'],
