        'lead' => 'IMEI registration for mobile devices made in or imported into India is done on the DoT’s Device Setu (ICDR) portal before sale or customs clearance. The portal issues an IMEI certificate listing the model and its IMEIs, which customs checks against each consignment.',
        'sections' => [
            ['IMEI certificate for customs', '<p>For imports, the IMEI certificate is generated on the ICDR portal for each consignment. It lists the device model, the IMEIs, the importer, the original equipment manufacturer and the customs broker (CHA). Customs officers verify the shipment against it during clearance, and the same set of IMEIs cannot be used for a second certificate. Read our guide to the <a href="/resources/blogs/imei-certificate-for-customs-clearance-in-india">IMEI certificate for customs clearance</a>.</p>'],
